builtin classes and interfaces (`stdClass`, `Closure`,\\\\n  1627\\\\t`Generator`, `Traversable`, `Iterator`, `IteratorAggregate`, `ArrayAccess`,\\\\n  1628\\\\t`Countable`, `Stringable`, `JsonSerializable`, `UnitEnum`, `BackedEnum`, the\\\\n  1629\\\\t`Throwable` hierarchy; `ArrayObject` deferred), the function table with the\\\\n  1630\\\\tsupported builtins and their by-reference positions, `$GLOBALS` from the\\\\n  1920\\\\t   `:yang.php/refusal`.\\\\n  1921\\\\t\\\\n  1922\\\\t## 12. Safepoints\\\\n  1923\\\\t\\\\n  1924\\\\t- `:loop` and `:call` hooks (`phpsp`) serve signals: `pcntl_signal` handlers\\\\n  1925\\\\t  run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, and\\\\n  1926\\\\t  `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode. A recursion-depth bound\\\\n  1927\\\\t  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off).\\\\n  1928\\\\t- `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP and so\\\\n  1929\\\\t  nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count\\\\n  1930\\\\t  budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text, a recorded departure\\\\n  1931\\\\t  (owner decision B8.5, corner C21). A composition may supply one non-negative\\\\n  1932\\\\t  integer budget per run; omission means unlimited. Each entry to a `:loop` or\\\\n  1933\\\\t  `:call` hook consumes one unit, and the hook after the last available unit\\\\n  1934\\\\t  raises `PHP Fatal error:  Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded`.\\\\n  1935\\\\t  This operational fatal is not guest-catchable and skips shutdown functions\\\\n  1936\\\\t  and destructors. It bounds execution between hooks, not wall-clock time or\\\\n  1937\\\\t  blocking host operations; no generic VM instructions are charged.\\\\n  1938\\\\t- **Statement ticks** (`declare(ticks=N)`, `register_tick_function`) need\\\\n  1939\\\\t  `:line` sites before non-lambda statement nodes. `yang.safepoint` currently\\\\n  1940\\\\t  refuses a selected site that is not a `:lambda` (`site-not-lambda`), and\\\\n  1941\\\\t  `:line` insertion is safepoint slice 3, which Python tracing also needs.\\\\n  1942\\\\t  Ticks therefore **depend on the shared `:line` extension**: P7 splits into\\\\n  1943\\\\t  P7-a (signals, no dependency) and P7-b (ticks, behind safepoint slice 3).\\\\n  1944\\\\t  Neither L1 to L4 nor this frontend extends `yang.safepoint`; the extension\\\\n  1945\\\\t  is the safepoint seat's.\\\\n  1946\\\\t- No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded, and one request is one task.\\\\n  1947\\\\t\\\\n  1948\\\\t## 13. Diagnostics\\\\n  1949\\\\t\\\\n  1950\\\\tCompile time: `:yang.php/syntax`; `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}`;\\\\n  1951\\\\t`:yang.php/not-php`; `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` (a warning);\\\\n  1952\\\\t`:yang.php/compile-error` for PHP's compile-time fatals (a function redeclared\\\\n  1953\\\\tin one unit, `break 0`, a duplicate parameter, `$this` reassignment, a\\\\n  1954\\\\tpositional argument after a named one). Run time: guest warnings, notices and\\\\n  1955\\\\tdeprecations as records on the guest-diagnostics stream; fatals as `Error`\\\\n  1956\\\\tthrows; the uncaught-exception text pinned. Operational failures stay\\\\n  1957\\\\toperational (`yang.antlr.md` section 11).\\\\n  1958\\\\t\\\\n  1959\\\\t## 14. The differential-corpus plan\\\\n  1960\\\\t\\\\n  1961\\\\t- **Oracle**: the pinned PHP 8.3.x CLI with the pinned ini. The comparison\\\\n  1962\\\\t  covers stdout and the diagnostics stream, rendered in PHP's `Warning: ... in\\\\n  1963\\\\t  <unit> on line N` form with the path replaced by the unit name and the line\\\\n  1964\\\\t  derived from the side table (owner decision 2 of `yang.antlr.md` 8.5.1\\\\n  1965\\\\t  reused), against PHP's stderr with paths normalized.\\\\n  1966\\\\t- **Groups**: juggling (every pair of the comparison matrix, numeric strings,\\\\n  1967\\\\t  arithmetic warnings and `TypeError`); arrays (key coercion, order, next\\\\n  1968\\\\t  index after unset, copy-on-write observable through references, nested\\\\n  1969\\\\t  writes, sort stability); references and lifecycle (section 4.6's three\\\\n  1970\\\\t  sources); strings (bytes, interpolation forms, heredoc indentation,\\\\n  2090\\\\t|       | `use`, constants, the autoload   | imports on Node and Dart with     |\\\\n  2091\\\\t|       | class map, publication and DHT   | equal output; the computed-path   |\\\\n  2092\\\\t|       | import parserless on Node and    | diagnostic; an unpublished target |\\\\n  2093\\\\t|       | Dart, the dynamic-scope profile  | refused at publication by name; a |\\\\n  2094\\\\t|       | for including functions          | pinned but unserved target:       |\\\\n  2095\\\\t|       |                                  | `include` warns and yields        |\\\\n  2096\\\\t|       |                                  | `false`, `require` and            |\\\\n  2097\\\\t|       |                                  | `require_once` throw `Error`; a   |\\\\n  2098\\\\t|       |                                  | refused `_once` retries delivery  |\\\\n  2099\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2100\\\\t| P7-a  | signals: `phpsp` hooks at        | a signal at a `:loop` hook runs   |\\\\n  2101\\\\t|       | `:loop` and `:call`,             | the handler; an empty signal      |\\\\n  2102\\\\t|       | `pcntl_signal`, the safepoint    | stream never parks; budget        |\\\\n  2103\\\\t|       | budget                           | exhaustion raises the pinned      |\\\\n  2104\\\\t|       |                                  | fatal text                        |\\\\n  2105\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2106\\\\t| P7-b  | ticks: `declare(ticks)`,         | tick counts equal PHP's for the   |\\\\n  2107\\\\t|       | `register_tick_function`; behind | statement fixture                 |\\\\n  2108\\\\t|       | safepoint slice 3                |                                   |\\\\n  2109\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2110\\\\t| P8    | legacy retirement: the legacy    | the REPL prints `1` for `<?php $x |\\\\n  2111\\\\t|       | test programs in the new corpus, | = 1; echo $x;`; every legacy test |\\\\n  2112\\\\t|       | the demo on checked-in CST       | program passes with corrected     |\\\\n  2113\\\\t|       | packets,                         | expectations; the demo runs its   |\\\\n  2114\\\\t|       | `src/dev/subsystems.edn`         | samples parserless in the         |\\\\n  2115\\\\t|       | retargeted, `yang/php.cljc`      | browser; no reference to the      |\\\\n  2116\\\\t|       | deleted, the compiler revision   | legacy `yang.php` namespace       |\\\\n  2117\\\\t|       | removed from the standard        | remains                           |\\\\n  2118\\\\t|       | catalog                          |                                   |\\\\n  2119\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2120\\\\t| P9    | builtin surface slices (strings  | each a corpus group with PHP      |\\\\n  2121\\\\t|       | II, arrays II, JSON, math II),   | parity; `eval` shares the         |\\\\n  2122\\\\t|       | `$$`, `extract`, `compact` and   | caller's symbol table; closes     |\\\\n  2123\\\\t|       | the dynamic scope, `eval` as a   | corners C5, C6 (prefer-ref), C11, |\\\\n  2124\\\\t|       | compilation request              | C12, C13                          |\\\\n  2125\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2126\\\\t\\\\n  2127\\\\tDeferred: `preg_*` (a portable regex engine), `mb_*`, `serialize`, Reflection,\\\\n  2128\\\\tSPL data structures, `DateTime` beyond the time effect, sessions, PDO and\\\\n  2129\\\\tevery `ext/*` surface (bound per ADR 0004), return by reference, `goto`, cycle\\\\n  2130\\\\tcollection (corner C1).\\\\n  2131\\\\t\\\\n  2132\\\\t## 16. The yang.core lift enumeration\\\\n  2133\\\\t\\\\n  2134\\\\tBeyond L1 to L4 (`yang.typescript.md` section 17), PHP requires nothing new.\\\\n  2135\\\\tIt exercises `yang.core.stage` (the ok-check on `:yang.cst/ok`),\\\\n  2425\\\\t|                     | root; optional absent imports are  |                  |\\\\n  2426\\\\t|                     | not publishable.                    |                  |\\\\n  2427\\\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\\\n  2428\\\\t| C39 default         | Engine: `spl_autoload_register(null)`| restricted;     |\\\\n  2429\\\\t| autoloader          | installs PHP's default loader. Here:| departure        |\\\\n  2430\\\\t|                     | the call is refused as              | `G-default-      |\\\\n  2431\\\\t|                     | `G-default-autoload`; Composer      | autoload`; class |\\\\n  2432\\\\t|                     | class-map data is allowed, its      | map data remains |\\\\n  2433\\\\t|                     | filesystem lookup is not.           | supported        |\\\\n  2434\\\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\\\n  2435\\\\t\\\\n  2436\\\\t### 17.3 Convergence and the blocking rule\\\\n  2437\\\\t\\\\n  2438\\\\t**Claimed rows are normative, and a known-incorrect claimed row blocks.** A\\\\n  2439\\\\trow of the transition table is a statement of Zend's behaviour, fixed from the\\\\n  2440\\\\thandler source and **confirmed by the oracle before the slice that claims it\\\\n  2441\\\\tlands**. After landing, a disagreement between a row and the pinned PHP CLI is\\\\n  2442\\\\ta defect of the row, never of the fixture. A finding that a claimed row\\\\n  2443\\\\tcontradicts Zend blocks landing of any slice whose support profile includes\\\\n  2444\\\\tthat row until either the row is corrected (and its fixture regenerated from\\\\n  2445\\\\tthe oracle), or the Architect explicitly moves the behaviour to section 17.2\\\\n  2446\\\\tas a restricted corner with a departure fixture whose expected value is the\\\\n  2447\\\\trecorded deviation, with the owner's acceptance when the corner touches a\\\\n  2448\\\\tPhase 3 exit criterion. Regenerating a fixture to match an incorrect row is\\\\n  2449\\\\tforbidden: oracle fixtures pin behaviour; they do not legitimize a\\\\n  2450\\\\tcontradictory normative rule.\\\\n  2451\\\\t\\\\n  2452\\\\tThe landing gate is therefore: every claimed-row fixture equals the oracle;\\\\n  2453\\\\tevery corner's departure fixture equals its recorded deviation; no fixture\\\\n  2454\\\\tfailure is unclassified. A new finding lands in one of four bins, in blocking\\\\n  2455\\\\torder:\\\\n  2456\\\\t\\\\n  2457\\\\t1. a defect in a claimed row (blocks);\\\\n  2458\\\\t2. a missing row required by an exit criterion or the C4 profile (blocks);\\\\n  2459\\\\t3. a reclassification request, row to corner (an Architect decision recorded\\\\n  2460\\\\t   in the ledger; blocks until decided);\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.6|eval|JVM|parse|compiler' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'php|source|JVM' src/cljc/yang/stage.cljc; rg --files src | rg 'yang/.+(parse|stage)|php'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.6|eval|JVM|parse|compiler' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'php|source|JVM' src/cljc/yang/stage.cljc; rg --files src | rg 'yang/.+(parse|stage)|php'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"8:pilot pipeline (parser stage, scope analysis, lowering, prelude;\\\\n40:8.11, and add cross-references from sections 8.6 and 8.9. Landed on\\\\n100:are compiled, through ANTLR-generated parsers hosted behind a stream\\\\n104:The architectural decision is to make Yang an **open compiler composition\\\\n111:ANTLR operates behind a stream boundary. Its generated parsers and\\\\n118:Remote compiler and content services use `dao.stream.remote` mirror and\\\\n140:Host parser interpreter / isolated ANTLR worker\\\\n167:The direct evaluator route and the macro route are composition\\\\n168:alternatives. A composition must not feed both into one evaluator and\\\\n195:  (`src/cljc/yang/php.cljc`) contain handwritten tokenizers, parsers, and\\\\n208:  unsuccessful appends; a general compiler pipeline needs explicit\\\\n230:   across durable or remote compiler boundaries.\\\\n246:The six non-negotiable invariants of `datom.world.md` bind the compiler\\\\n252:- **No implicit control flow:** admission, parse completion, retries,\\\\n257:- **No shared mutable state:** compiler state is immutable and threaded\\\\n260:- **No collapse of interpretation and execution:** streams do not parse,\\\\n261:  compile, schedule, or evaluate; compilation does not execute the\\\\n275:1. **Grammar package:** lexer/parser grammars, imports, token vocabulary,\\\\n277:2. **Syntax export profile:** how the generated parser's CST becomes\\\\n295:  :yang.grammar/parser \\\\\\\"RubyParser\\\\\\\"\\\\n313:- Generated JVM classes, JavaScript modules, or Dart libraries.\\\\n315:- Any target-specific lexer/parser helper implementation.\\\\n336:    \\\\\\\"The :yang.frontend/grammar map: package address, lexer and parser\\\\n375:The composition supplies the catalog to the compiler coordinator. A\\\\n385:option, or unavailable parser implementation produces a qualified\\\\n386:compiler outcome. None causes automatic dependency downloading or\\\\n435:silently drops children is not acceptable compiler behavior.\\\\n454:AST grammar, or evaluator di