   79\\\\t :license {\\\\\\\"PhpLexer.g4\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"MIT (header: Copyright (c) 2015-2019 Ivan Kochurkin, Positive Technologies; (c) 2019 Thierry Marianne); vendored with its notice verbatim\\\\\\\",\\\\n    80\\\\t           \\\\\\\"PhpParser.g4\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"MIT (header: Copyright (c) 2015-2019 Ivan Kochurkin, Positive Technologies; (c) 2019 Thierry Marianne); vendored with its notice verbatim\\\\\\\",\\\\n    81\\\\t           \\\\\\\"Java/PhpLexerBase.java\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"MIT (header: Copyright (c) 2015-2019 Ivan Kochurkin, Positive Technologies; (c) 2019 Thierry Marianne); vendored with its notice verbatim\\\\\\\",\\\\n    82\\\\t           \\\\\\\"antlr4-runtime 4.13.2\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"BSD-3-Clause\\\\\\\"},\\\\n    83\\\\t :redistribution {:vendored-sources [\\\\\\\"antlr/php/PhpLexer.g4\\\\\\\"\\\\n    84\\\\t                                     \\\\\\\"antlr/php/PhpParser.g4\\\\\\\"\\\\n    85\\\\t                                     \\\\\\\"antlr/php/PhpLexerBase.java\\\\\\\"],\\\\n    86\\\\t                  :generated-artifacts :none}}\\\\n    20\\\\t   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\\\\n    21\\\\t3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\\\\n    22\\\\t4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\n    24\\\\t## Non-Negotiable Invariants\\\\n    25\\\\t\\\\n    26\\\\t- Do not introduce hidden global state.\\\\n    27\\\\t- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\\\\n    28\\\\t- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\\\\n    29\\\\t- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\\\\n    30\\\\t- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\\\\n    31\\\\t- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\\\\n    32\\\\t- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\\\\n    33\\\\t\\\\n    34\\\\t## Tuples and Datoms\\\\n    35\\\\t\\\\n   125\\\\t- When uncertain, ask at the architectural level, not the implementation level.\\\\n   126\\\\t- Explanations should align with Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp lineage.\\\\n   127\\\\t- Program store writes go through `engine/store-put`; any other store write\\\\n   128\\\\t  the store-write audit (`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`)\\\\n   129\\\\t  detects must be on its allowlist; its docstring states the residual it\\\\n   130\\\\t  leaves to review.\\\\n   131\\\\t\\\\n   132\\\\t### Problem Decomposition\\\\n   133\\\\t\\\\n   134\\\\tIf a problem appears complex:\\\\n   135\\\\t1. Decompose it into streams.\\\\n   136\\\\t2. Identify invariants.\\\\n   137\\\\t3. Restrict degrees of freedom.\\\\n   138\\\\t4. Make causality explicit.\\\\n   139\\\\t5. Let structure emerge from constraints.\\\\n   140\\\\t\\\\n   141\\\\t## Operational & Specialized Guides\\\\n   142\\\\t\\\\n   143\\\\t- **Advanced Concepts**: See [`docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`](../agents/advanced-concepts.md) for parallel transport, capability tokens, and entanglement.\\\\n   144\\\\t- **Build & Test**: See [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../agents/build-n-test.md) for build, lint, and test commands and TDD guidelines.\\\\n   145\\\\t- **Engineering Team Roster**: See [`docs/agents/team.md`](../agents/team.md) for engineering team roles and LLM model assignments.\\\\n   146\\\\t- **Agent Delegation**: See [`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../agents/roles/orchestrator.md) for collaboration protocols and delegating tasks or reviews through `agy`, `cmd`, `glm`, `deepseek`, and `codex`; each orchestrator session has its own append-only log at `orchestrator-logs/<unix-time-stamp>-<brief-orchestrator-descriptive-name>.md` under the repository root.\\\\n   147\\\\t- **Website & Content**: See [`docs/agents/format.md`](../agents/format.md) for `.chp` and `.blog` EDN/Hiccup file specifications.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files test/yang/php/antlr | head -65; rg -n 'source-envelope|execution-budget|safepoint/program|hooks/program|phpsp|derive' test/yang/php src/cljc/yang/php* src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc; rg -n 'eval|compile|load|stream/(append|read)|program' src/cljc/yin/vm/primitives* src/cljc/yin/vm/module* src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/*.cljc | head -130\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files test/yang/php/antlr | head -65; rg -n 'source-envelope|execution-budget|safepoint/program|hooks/program|phpsp|derive' test/yang/php src/cljc/yang/php* src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc; rg -n 'eval|compile|load|stream/(append|read)|program' src/cljc/yin/vm/primitives* src/cljc/yin/vm/module* src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/*.cljc | head -130\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"test/yang/php/antlr/scope_test.clj\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p3b.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/permutation_oracle_quick.edn\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p9.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/php/ant